"""later_register.py — the Round-11 later-phase register (COV-10; plan §15; SEED-14a, Stage B T4).

The ratified Round-11 plan (``PD/NEXT_PHASE_PLAN.md`` §15) defers twenty catalog units (``LATER-nn``) and
the S1b universe disposes 153 items as ``later-phase``. COV-10 requires every one of them to be *recorded*
with its trigger and date — "a deferral that is not in that file did not happen" (AGENTS.md gotcha 8) —
by a committed, deterministic generator. This tool is that generator. It reads only committed inputs:

* ``PD/data/round11_plan.csv`` — the unit list (``sub_round == later``) and the units moved into Round 11
  at S6 (``sub_round`` ``moved (S6) -> <rows>``);
* ``PD/data/ticket_catalog.csv`` — each unit's catalog gate (``operator_gate``);
* ``PD/NEXT_PHASE_PLAN.md`` — §15's table (what · trigger · runs · $/mo) and the GATE-P time in its header;
* ``PD/universe/UNIVERSE_DISPOSED.csv`` — every ``later-phase`` item with its trigger;
* ``PD/data/decision_catalog.csv`` — the operator answers (``operator_answer``, ``answered_at``) that
  re-disposition an item into or out of the later phase (plan §9.1/§9.2/§15).

and writes:

1. ``docs/build/reports/later-register/LATER_REGISTER.md`` and ``later_register.csv`` — the full register
   (every unit, every item, its trigger, date and Round-11 status), regenerated byte-for-byte;
2. an appended ``## Later-phase register (Round 11)`` section at the end of ``docs/tickets/DEFERRALS.md`` —
   one owed row per later-phase unit (``D-R11-LATER-nn``) with ``owner:``/``trigger:`` in ``unblocked by``
   (DEFERRALS rule 5) and a ``BL-nnn`` home. The section is **append-once**: a later run never rewrites
   it; a unit that appears later is appended under an ``### … additions`` heading. Rows only grow.

Usage::

    python3 docs/build/tools/later_register.py --recorded-at "$(date -u +%FT%TZ)"   # write (idempotent)
    python3 docs/build/tools/later_register.py --check                             # verify; exit 1 on drift

``--check`` regenerates the register in memory and requires the committed files to be byte-identical, and
requires every expected DEFERRALS row to exist with each generated cell's text still contained in the
row's cell (an appended annotation is allowed; a rewrite is not). Exit codes: 0 ok · 1 drift/missing ·
2 input error. Stdlib only; runs on Python 3.9+.

Owners, kinds, backlog homes and due-date wording per unit (``UNIT_META``) are this unit's reading of the
plan (agent interpretation, labelled as such in the output); triggers, costs and answers are quoted from
the inputs.
"""

